.TH "REPROCTL\-HELP\-EXIT\-CODES" "7" "2026" "reproctl" "Repro Development Tools"
.SH NAME
reproctl\-help\-exit\-codes \- exit codes returned by reproctl commands
.SH DESCRIPTION
reproctl uses a small set of exit codes consistently across all
commands.
Scripts and CI pipelines can rely on these values to distinguish between
different failure modes.
.SH EXIT CODES
.TP
\f[B]0\f[R]
Success.
The command completed without errors.
.TP
\f[B]1\f[R]
Error.
The command failed due to a runtime error, invalid input, or an
unrecoverable condition.
.TP
\f[B]2\f[R]
User cancelled.
The user aborted an interactive prompt or confirmation dialog (e.g.,
answering \(dqno\(dq to a destructive operation).
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
reproctl db reset
case $? in
  0) echo \(dqDatabase reset successfully\(dq ;;
  1) echo \(dqReset failed\(dq ;;
  2) echo \(dqReset cancelled by user\(dq ;;
esac
.EE
